Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: flush after a successful capture pause

The capture STOP sequence introduced by local patch 0018 tests !ret before
queuing FLUSH. q6asm_cmd_nowait() returns apr_send_pkt() directly; that
function returns the positive packet size on a successful rpmsg send.
Consequently the usual successful PAUSE never reaches FLUSH.

Accept any nonnegative result, retaining the existing error propagation and
playback EOS behavior. Do not change the audio client's setup lifetime or
the synchronous command path. Hardware capture reopen testing is required.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -356,7 +356,8 @@
 		if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
 			ret = q6asm_cmd_nowait(prtd->audio_client,
 					       prtd->stream_id, CMD_PAUSE);
-			if (!ret)
+			/* APR returns the packet size on a successful send. */
+			if (ret >= 0)
 				ret = q6asm_cmd_nowait(prtd->audio_client,
 						       prtd->stream_id,
 						       CMD_FLUSH);
